\tag{ftip}
\tag{rlvr}
\tag{evidence}

\card{Remark}{Rule, test, and proof evidence}{
\p{We synthesize three common evidence routes. Rule evidence compares a parsed
answer or format with a declared target, as in
\citet{Section 2.2}{guo2025deepseek}. Test evidence executes a candidate in a
sandbox and records test outcomes. Proof evidence submits a term to a specified
checker and records acceptance or an error.}

\p{These routes expose different predicates and costs. A rule can ignore the
derivation, a test suite can omit behavior, and a proof checker establishes
only the proposition and trusted-kernel boundary it was given. Their rewards
must not be merged without retaining which evidence source fired.}
}
